[46.479149, "o", " the same transaction id.\r\n467:\r\n\r\n=== Brief 03: lines 468-478 (show first ~220 lines) ===\r\n468:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n469:\r\n470:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n471:\r\n472:The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n473:messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n474:`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n475:equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n476:apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n477:after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n478:\r\n\r\n=== Brief 03: lines 479-684 (show first ~220 lines) ===\r\n479:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — field notes\r\n480:\r\n481:Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction sh"]
