[95.85957, "o", "Brief 09 lines 1670-1681\r\n1670:## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n1671:\r\n1672:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n1673:\r\n1674:Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n1675:amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n1676:only, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n1677:ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n1678:in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n1679:before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n1680:mail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n1681:\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@0f1e383a7916:/app# "]
