[180.28372, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         continue\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[180.283762, "o", ">     start=starts[0]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     end=len(lines)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for i in range(start+1,len(lines)+1):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         if re.match(r'^#+\\s*Investigation Brief\\s*\\d+\\b', lines[i-1]):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>             end=i-1; break\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     print(f\"\\n=== Brief {n:02d} lines {start}-{end} (show up to 200 lines) ===\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for j in range(start, min(end, start+199)+1):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         print(f\"{j}:\"+lines[j-1].rstrip('\\n'))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[180.33993, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 01 lines 11-27 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n11:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing\r\n12:\r\n13:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n14:\r\n15:Finance QA traced rerun drift to parsers that latched onto the wrong ledger\r\n16:slice. For extractor output, treat only the markdown section whose heading\r\n17:line is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also\r\n18:contains a working-copy ledger and prose that mentions ledger headings; those\r\n19:are investigative context only.\r\n20:\r\n21:Ignore any ledger block that includes a line `provisional: true` (case\r\n22:insensitive). When the same transaction id appears in multiple non-provisional\r\n23:ledger blocks, the last such block in file order is the base row for that id.\r\n24:\r\n25:Locate section boundaries with regular expressions anchored to whole heading\r\n26:lines at line start. Do not locate sections with indexOf or substring search.\r\n27:\r\n"]
[180.34941, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 02 lines 252-261 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n252:## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n253:\r\n254:Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n255:\r\n256:Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n257:amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n258:output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n259:rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n260:contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n261:\r\n"]
[180.351235, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 03 lines 468-478 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n468:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n469:\r\n470:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n471:\r\n472:The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n473:messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n474:`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n475:equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n476:apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n477:after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n478:\r\n"]
[180.351991, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 04 lines 685-695 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n685:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n686:\r\n687:Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n688:\r\n689:The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n690:target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n691:greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n692:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n693:applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n694:both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n695:\r\n"]
[180.353337, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 05 lines 828-837 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n828:## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n829:\r\n830:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n831:\r\n832:Committee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n833:default. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace\r\n834:owner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n835:`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n836:ledger date for the transaction.\r\n837:\r\n"]
[180.354648, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 06 lines 1058-1068 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n"]
[180.356262, "o", "1058:## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n1059:\r\n1060:Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n1061:\r\n1062:Auditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n1063:ledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n1064:sets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n1065:`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n1066:keep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n1067:places in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n1068:\r\n"]
[180.358691, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 07 lines 1201-1212 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n1201:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n"]
[180.358848, "o", "1202:\r\n1203:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n1204:\r\n1205:Exception coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n1206:`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n1207:when final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n1208:that transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n1209:comparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n1210:(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n1211:lexical order of the reason codes.\r\n1212:\r\n"]
[180.363028, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 08 lines 1419-1439 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n1419:## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n1420:\r\n1421:Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n1422:\r\n1423:Continued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n1424:`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n1425:with `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n1426:final status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n1427:notice changed status for that transaction.\r\n1428:\r\n1429:`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n1430:by `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n1431:(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n1432:semicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n1433:transaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n1434:same rows; leave exception_reason blank whe"]
[180.366166, "o", "n null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n1435:`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n1436:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n1437:notice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n1438:by notice_id ascending.\r\n1439:\r\n\r\n=== Brief 09 lines 1670-1681 (show up to 200 lines) ===\r\n1670:## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n1671:\r\n1672:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n1673:\r\n1674:Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n1675:amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n1676:only, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n1677:ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n1678:in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n1679:before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n1680:mail-driven status chan"]
[180.366277, "o", "ges; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n1681:\r\n"]
[180.383847, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[180.385698, "o", "root@0f1e383a7916:/app# "]
[194.423472, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\npath='/app/data/audit_archive.md'\nwith open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    lines=f.readlines()\nfor n in range(1,8):\n    pat=re.compile(r'^#+\\s*Investigation Brief\\s*0?%d\\b'%n)\n    starts=[i for i,l in enumerate(lines,1) if pat.match(l)]\n    if not starts:\n        print('Brief',n,'not found');\n        continue\n    start=starts[0]\n    end=len(lines)\n    for i in range(start+1,len(lines)+1):\n        if re.match(r'^#+\\s*Investigation Brief\\s*\\d+\\b', lines[i-1]):\n            end=i-1; break\n    print(f\"\\n=== Brief {n:02d} lines {start}-{end} ===\")\n    for j in range(start, end+1):\n        print(f\"{j}:\"+lines[j-1].rstrip('\\n'))\nPY\n"]
[194.424067, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> import re\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[194.424093, "o", "path='/app/data/audit_archive.md'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[194.424189, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[194.430606, "o", "> with open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     lines=f.readlines()\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> for n in range(1,8):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     pat=re.compile(r'^#+\\s*Investigation Brief\\s*0?%d\\b'%n)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     starts=[i for i,l in enumerate(lines,1) if pat.match(l)]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     if not starts:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         print('Brief',n,'not found');\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         continue\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     start=starts[0]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     end=len(lines)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for i in range(start+1,len(lines)+1):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         if re.match(r'^#+\\s*Investigation Brief\\s*\\d+\\b', lines[i-1]):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>             end=i-1; break\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     print(f\"\\n=== Brief {n:02d} lines {start}-{end} ===\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for j in range(start, end+1):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         print(f\"{j}:\"+lines[j-1].rstrip('\\n'))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[194.479755, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 01 lines 11-27 ==="]
[194.483183, "o", "\r\n11:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing\r\n12:\r\n13:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n14:\r\n15:Finance QA traced rerun drift to parsers that latched onto the wrong ledger\r\n16:slice. For extractor output, treat only the markdown section whose heading\r\n17:line is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also\r\n18:contains a working-copy ledger and prose that mentions ledger headings; those\r\n19:are investigative context only.\r\n20:\r\n21:Ignore any ledger block that includes a line `provisional: true` (case\r\n22:insensitive). When the same transaction id appears in multiple non-provisional\r\n23:ledger blocks, the last such block in file order is the base row for that id.\r\n24:\r\n25:Locate section boundaries with regular expressions anchored to whole heading\r\n26:lines at line start. Do not locate sections with indexOf or substring search.\r\n27:\r\n"]
[194.487495, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 02 lines 252-261 ===\r\n252:## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n253:\r\n254:Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n255:\r\n256:Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n257:amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n258:output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n259:rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n260:contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n261:\r\n"]
[194.491373, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 03 lines 468-478 ===\r\n468:## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n469:\r\n470:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n471:\r\n472:The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n473:messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n474:`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n475:equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n476:apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n477:after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n478:\r\n"]
[194.495728, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 04 lines 685-695 ===\r\n685:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n686:\r\n687:Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n688:\r\n689:The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n690:target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n"]
[194.496438, "o", "691:greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n692:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n693:applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n694:both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n695:\r\n"]
[194.5009, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 05 lines 828-837 ===\r\n828:## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n829:\r\n830:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n831:\r\n832:Committee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n833:default. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace\r\n834:owner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n835:`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n836:ledger date for the transaction.\r\n837:\r\n"]
[194.502234, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 06 lines 1058-1068 ===\r\n1058:## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n1059:\r\n1060:Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n1061:\r\n1062:Auditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n1063:ledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n1064:sets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n1065:`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n1066:keep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n1067:places in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n1068:\r\n"]
[194.505003, "o", "\r\n=== Brief 07 lines 1201-1212 ==="]
[194.505211, "o", "\r\n1201:## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n1202:\r\n1203:Extract policy (authoritative):\r\n1204:\r\n1205:Exception coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n1206:`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n1207:when final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n1208:that transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n1209:comparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n1210:(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n1211:lexical order of the reason codes.\r\n1212:\r\n"]
[194.513518, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0f1e383a7916:/app# "]
[195.179216, "i", "sed -n '1,340p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/sections.js\n"]
[195.181528, "o", "sed -n '1,340p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/sections.js\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[195.192023, "o", "const { parseLedger } = require(\"./ledger\");\r\r\nconst { parseMeetings } = require(\"./meetings\");\r\r\nconst { parseEmails } = require(\"./emails\");\r\r\nconst { parseCorrections } = require(\"./corrections\");\r\r\nconst { parsePolicyExceptions } = require(\"./policy\");\r\r\n\r\r\nfunction parseArchive(markdown) {\r\r\n  return {\r\r\n    ledger: parseLedger(markdown),\r\r\n    meetings: parseMeetings(markdown),\r\r\n    emails: parseEmails(markdown),\r\r\n    corrections: parseCorrections(markdown),\r\r\n    policyExceptions: parsePolicyExceptions(markdown),\r\r\n  };\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parseArchive };\r\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@0f1e383a7916:/app# "]
[196.008452, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/emails.js\n"]
[196.010148, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/emails.js\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[196.023482, "o", "function parseEmails(markdown) {\r\r\n  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Email Excerpts\");\r\r\n  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Policy Exceptions\");\r\r\n  const slice =\r\r\n    start >= 0 && end > start ? markdown.slice(start, end) : markdown;\r\r\n  const emails = [];\r\r\n  const blocks = slice.split(/\\n\\n+/);\r\r\n  for (const block of blocks) {\r\r\n    const fromMatch = block.match(/^From:\\s*(.+)$/im);\r\r\n    const subjectMatch = block.match(/^Subject:\\s*Re:\\s*(TXN-[0-9a-f-]+)/im);\r\r\n    const statusMatch = block.match(/^status:\\s*(\\w+)/im);\r\r\n    if (!fromMatch || !subjectMatch || !statusMatch) {\r\r\n      continue;\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    emails.push({\r\r\n      from_addr: fromMatch[1].trim(),\r\r\n      transaction_id: subjectMatch[1],\r\r\n      status: statusMatch[1].trim().toLowerCase(),\r\r\n    });\r\r\n  }\r\r\n"]
[196.02461, "o", "  return emails;\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parseEmails };\r\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[196.025134, "o", "root@0f1e383a7916:/app# "]
[196.828634, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js\n"]
[196.829434, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js"]
[196.834068, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[196.84168, "o", "function parsePolicyExceptions(markdown) {\r\r\n"]
[196.841871, "o", "  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Policy Exceptions\");\r\r\n"]
[196.84191, "o", "  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Correction Notices\");\r\r\n"]
[196.842343, "o", "  const slice =\r\r\n    start >= 0 && end > start ? markdown.slice(start, end) : \"\";\r\r\n  const ids = new Set();\r\r\n  const re = /^transaction:\\s*(TXN-[0-9a-f-]+)\\s*$/gim;\r\r\n  let match;\r\r\n  while ((match = re.exec(slice)) !== null) {\r\r\n"]
[196.842745, "o", "    ids.add(match[1]);\r\r\n  }\r\r\n  return ids;\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parsePolicyExceptions };\r\r\n"]
